Subject: [PATCH 10/12] R80b, part 2, patch 10 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M14; Review 80, the SM seat's findings 22, 23 and 24 and a reader's two
 derivations; main checked 23 and 24 and the derivations with a computation of
 its own, and did not check 22): FOUR THINGS SAID OF B1895 ARE COMPUTED IN ITS
 LOCK, AND NOTED ON ITS PAGE.

THE COMPUTATIONS ARE MAIN'S (the arc B1898 keeps the script and its output). Run again here it gives the same output. They are placed in the lock, so that each note of the page is held to a computation.

1. ROW A1 (finding 23). The statement is true and was not what was computed: the script and the lock compared the outcome of two tests and built no word of the second convention. The lock builds it, letter by letter over the integers: it is the seat's word conjugated by the swap on 1,332 of 1,332 sequences. A control with the letters exchanged differs.
2. REVERSAL (finding 24). The seventh section left it as not computed. For each of the four marks that do not annihilate their own line, 358 or 362 of the 1,332 sequences are allowed differently from their reversal; for the two that do, none.
3. THE SECOND LEAST READING (the second derivation). Over 3,378 primitive cyclic run sequences the least reading is the all-ones', the second least the all-twos', and every other reads above 17/12, the least of them 1.4866 at (1, 1, 2, 2). The reader's argument by cases for every sequence was read by main; it is not written in the arc and the lock does not hold it. The first derivation is the page's rows A5 and A6.
4. THE LOCK'S OWN SENTENCE (finding 22, not checked by main; counted in the test). It said its sequences were ones the arc's script did not try. Of its 409 distinct sequences 295 were tried; 114 are new.

NOTED, each with the sentence before it kept: under the table of the third section; twice in the seventh section; in the lock's docstring; in register row P-819, where (3) is computed and (1) has main's computation. Whether that row is done is main's. No number is this seat's: each is main's, or is counted by the test.

The locks of B1881, B1895 and B1897 pass: 17, 10 and 4 tests. 0 of 19.
